      "message": "It would seem better to have this be called getDeviceConfigIntProperty. Otherwise we end up having multiple getDeviceConfigProperty methods that differ only in the return type. This could get confusing for two reasons.\n\n1. There is only one getDeviceConfigProperty method that returns a string.\n2. Overloading only by the return value is error prone. Not so much for String and int, but\n   consider, for example, if we had two methods one returning a long and one an int (or one\n   a float and one an int). It would be very difficult to tell which method is in use.\n\nSuggest renaming to getDeviceConfigPropertyInt or similar. Or, be consistent with DeviceConfig, which also does not use overloading only on the return value, instead providing getString, getInt, getBoolean, etc.\n\nAlso, why is this method not in NetworkStackUtils? Surely we\u0027ll need to get int properties elsewhere in the network stack at some point in the future?",
